<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Civita Castellana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Civita Castellana is a town in the province of Viterbo in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lazio">Lazio</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, built on a tufa plateau above deep ravines. It stands on the site of Falerii, the chief town of the Faliscans, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> destroyed in 241 BCE, moving its people to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/falerii-novi">Falerii Novi</a> on the plain. The site was resettled in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and has a Romanesque cathedral.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/civita-castellana.jpg" alt="Civita Castellana" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CIVITACASTELLANA at Italian Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Civita_Castellana_(VT)_-_piazza_Giacomo_Matteotti_-_vista_notturna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
